WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.223 --> 00:00:02.315
- Collecting milk bottles,

00:00:02.315 --> 00:00:03.742
following brown road signs,

00:00:03.742 --> 00:00:05.196
spotting village water pumps,

00:00:05.196 --> 00:00:06.756
taking pictures of tombstones,

00:00:06.756 --> 00:00:08.678
appreciating round-abouts...

00:00:08.678 --> 00:00:10.915
These are dull things to do, aren't they?

00:00:10.915 --> 00:00:13.769
Welcome to the Dull Men's Club?

00:00:13.769 --> 00:00:15.115
(music)

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:17.143
(ding)

00:00:17.143 --> 00:00:18.639
I am Grover Click.

00:00:18.639 --> 00:00:20.908
I'm assistant vice president
of the Dull Men's Club

00:00:20.908 --> 00:00:23.323
and one of its founders.

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:25.543
The Dull Men's Club is a
group that get together

00:00:25.543 --> 00:00:27.282
to celebrate the ordinary.

00:00:27.282 --> 00:00:29.830
Eh, it began in the
1980s, a long time ago.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:34.793
We began in New York City,
and later I moved to London,

00:00:34.793 --> 00:00:36.569
and the Dull Men's Club followed me

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:39.484
and has grown here in England as well.

00:00:39.484 --> 00:00:42.266
It's got members both
in England and America

00:00:42.266 --> 00:00:44.228
and across the world.

00:00:44.228 --> 00:00:45.845
The last time we did a round-up,

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.029
putting all things together,

00:00:47.029 --> 00:00:49.197
it looked like we had about 5,000 members.

00:00:49.197 --> 00:00:50.873
So here are the people that do things

00:00:50.873 --> 00:00:52.742
that some people think are dull.

00:00:52.742 --> 00:00:54.253
Here's Steve:

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:57.090
- Hi, I'm a milk bottle collector.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.683
I have some 20,000 milk bottles

00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:00.385
from not just the UK
but all over the world:

00:01:00.385 --> 00:01:04.450
Germany, France, South
Africa, Hong Kong, Portugal.

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:06.748
I've got Iranian bottles.

00:01:06.748 --> 00:01:09.165
Uh, I don't like milk at all.

00:01:11.121 --> 00:01:12.254
I just don't like it.

00:01:12.254 --> 00:01:14.094
(laughing)

00:01:14.094 --> 00:01:15.087
- [Mr. Click] And we have some women

00:01:15.087 --> 00:01:17.111
that are interested interested
in the Dull Men's Club.

00:01:17.111 --> 00:01:18.309
Here's Amanda:

00:01:18.309 --> 00:01:22.644
- My quirky hobby is randomly
following brown tourist signs.

00:01:22.644 --> 00:01:24.062
- Yep, you heard her right.

00:01:24.062 --> 00:01:26.372
- I get inspired to turn off
the road whenever I see one.

00:01:26.372 --> 00:01:28.148
I found it very hard not to.

00:01:28.148 --> 00:01:30.031
I follow brown signs around the UK,

00:01:30.031 --> 00:01:31.907
and indeed, the whole world.

00:01:31.907 --> 00:01:34.997
So, I've now been to
thousands and thousands.

00:01:34.997 --> 00:01:36.955
- [Mr. Click] We also have a member

00:01:36.955 --> 00:01:37.788
that appreciates round-abouts.

00:01:37.788 --> 00:01:41.221
- I'm Kevin, and I'm the president

00:01:41.221 --> 00:01:45.401
of the UK Roundabout Appreciation Society,

00:01:45.401 --> 00:01:49.363
also known as Lord of the
Rings, that's my official title.

00:01:49.363 --> 00:01:52.228
I have taken thousands of
pictures of round-abouts

00:01:52.228 --> 00:01:54.174
even when I'm abroad on holiday.

00:01:54.174 --> 00:01:57.456
I know a lot of people would
find my hobby quite dull,

00:01:57.456 --> 00:01:59.301
but it's bright being dull.

00:01:59.301 --> 00:02:01.462
It's sexy being dull.

00:02:01.462 --> 00:02:03.695
- And next is a member that is just dying

00:02:03.695 --> 00:02:05.413
to get into a graveyard.

00:02:05.413 --> 00:02:06.725
(screeching sound)

00:02:06.725 --> 00:02:09.786
(woeful music)

00:02:09.786 --> 00:02:12.713
- I'm a tomb traveler, and I take pictures

00:02:12.713 --> 00:02:14.644
of famous graves around the globe.

00:02:14.644 --> 00:02:16.675
I probably have at least
four or five hundred

00:02:16.675 --> 00:02:18.010
on various parts of the world:

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:20.911
Kennedy, Martin Luther King,
Bruce Lee and Brandon Lee,

00:02:20.911 --> 00:02:23.998
Elvis Presley, Ludwig van
Beethoven, Charlie Chaplin.

00:02:23.998 --> 00:02:26.180
Well, I don't feel that I'm a dull man,

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.555
but people have said that,
but I prefer to think

00:02:28.555 --> 00:02:30.759
that I’ve got a rounded,
albeit interesting way

00:02:30.759 --> 00:02:33.226
to take my mind away from work.

00:02:33.226 --> 00:02:35.943
- And we have Dick, who is
spotting village water pumps.

00:02:35.943 --> 00:02:37.440
- And it all came about by accident.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.215
Ten years ago, somebody pointed out

00:02:39.215 --> 00:02:41.106
a tiny little pump by
the side of the road,

00:02:41.106 --> 00:02:43.647
and almost every village you went through

00:02:43.647 --> 00:02:46.696
I'd say, "There's a pump,"
and we'd slam the brakes on,

00:02:46.696 --> 00:02:48.380
jump out and take a picture of the pump.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:50.111
- It's okay to be dull.

00:02:50.111 --> 00:02:52.338
There are a lot of studies being done now

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:55.098
that boredom has got benefits.

00:02:55.098 --> 00:02:57.409
We're not so interested
in the glitz and glam;

00:02:57.409 --> 00:03:00.897
we're quite happy with
simple things in life.

00:03:00.897 --> 00:03:03.897
(upbeat jazz music)

